Task 3: Network Interface Optimization with ethtool
Subtask 3.1: Optimize Ring Buffer Sizes
INTERFACE=$(ip route | grep default | awk '{print $5}' | head -1)
echo "Current ring buffer settings for $INTERFACE:"
ethtool -g $INTERFACE

cat > ~/optimize_ring_buffers.sh << 'EOF'
#!/bin/bash
INTERFACE=$(ip route | grep default | awk '{print $5}' | head -1)

echo "Optimizing ring buffers for interface: $INTERFACE"

MAX_RX=$(ethtool -g $INTERFACE | awk '/Pre-set maximums/{f=1} f && /^RX:/{print $2; exit}')
MAX_TX=$(ethtool -g $INTERFACE | awk '/Pre-set maximums/{f=1} f && /^TX:/{print $2; exit}')

echo "Maximum RX ring buffer: $MAX_RX"
echo "Maximum TX ring buffer: $MAX_TX"

if [ -n "$MAX_RX" ] && [ "$MAX_RX" != "n/a" ]; then
    sudo ethtool -G $INTERFACE rx $MAX_RX
fi

if [ -n "$MAX_TX" ] && [ "$MAX_TX" != "n/a" ]; then
    sudo ethtool -G $INTERFACE tx $MAX_TX
fi

echo "New ring buffer settings:"
ethtool -g $INTERFACE
EOF

chmod +x ~/optimize_ring_buffers.sh
~/optimize_ring_buffers.sh
Deliverable 3.1: ethtool -g $INTERFACE output shows "Current hardware settings" RX/TX values equal to the "Pre-set maximums" values (unless the NIC driver is virtual and does not support resizing, in which case the script should print not supported and the student notes this in their results file).

